From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wsock32: WSARecvEx partial flag, GetAddressByName (3589)

wsock32: WSARecvEx partial flag, GetAddressByName

WSARecvEx reports a datagram larger than the buffer as MSG_PARTIAL (the buffer is filled and the length returned
instead of WSAEMSGSIZE) and fails a NULL flags pointer. GetAddressByNameA/W resolve a host name for the DNS name
space into CSADDR_INFO structures, one per address and requested protocol (TCP by default), packed with their
socket addresses into the caller's buffer; a short buffer gives ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and the needed size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---
diff --git a/dlls/wsock32/service.c b/dlls/wsock32/service.c
index c109511..56a5740 100644
--- a/dlls/wsock32/service.c
+++ b/dlls/wsock32/service.c
@@ -19,11 +19,14 @@
  */
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 #include "windef.h"
 #include "winbase.h"
 #include "winerror.h"
 #include "winsock2.h"
+#include "ws2tcpip.h"
 #include "wtypes.h"
